{"name":"Pastel de Nata","hex":"#f2c975","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pastel de nata","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Portuguese custard tart"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastel_de_nata"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pastel de nata","blocks":[{"text":"Pastel de nata is a Portuguese egg custard tart pastry, optionally dusted with cinnamon. Outside Portugal, they are particularly popular in other parts of Western Europe, former Portuguese colonies, such as Brazil, Mozambique, Macau, Goa, Malacca and Timor-Leste, and other parts of Asia. The Macau variant has been adopted by KFC and is available in regions such as mainland China, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Thailand, South Korea, Singapore and Malaysia. In Indonesia, this pastry is especially popular in Kampung Tugu, Jakarta, a culturally Portuguese (Mardijker) enclave."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Pasteis_de_Belem.jpg/330px-Pasteis_de_Belem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel_de_nata","wikidata":"Q1421401"},{"title":"Pastel","blocks":[{"text":"A pastel is an art medium that consists of powdered pigment and a binder. It can exist in a variety of forms, including a stick, a square, a pebble, and a pan of color, among other forms. The pigments used in pastels are similar to those used to produce some other colored visual arts media, such as oil paints; the binder is of a neutral hue and low saturation. The color effect of pastels is closer to the natural dry pigments than that of any other process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/William_Merritt_Chase%2C_Study_of_Flesh_Color_and_Gold%2C_1888%2C_NGA_103252.jpg/330px-William_Merritt_Chase%2C_Study_of_Flesh_Color_and_Gold%2C_1888%2C_NGA_103252.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel","wikidata":"Q189085"},{"title":"Pastel (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Pastels or pastel colors belong to a pale family of colors, which, when described in the HSV color space, have high value and low or medium saturation. They are named after the artistic medium made from pigment and solid binding agents, similar to crayons. Pastel sticks historically had lower saturation than paints of the same pigment, hence the name of this color family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Commercial_pastels.JPG/330px-Commercial_pastels.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastel_(color)","wikidata":"Q2513175"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tart_telur_Portugis_%28Past%C3%A9is_de_nata%29_20230409_194702.jpg/500px-Tart_telur_Portugis_%28Past%C3%A9is_de_nata%29_20230409_194702.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tart_telur_Portugis_%28Past%C3%A9is_de_nata%29_20230409_194702.jpg/1280px-Tart_telur_Portugis_%28Past%C3%A9is_de_nata%29_20230409_194702.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Tart_telur_Portugis_%28Past%C3%A9is_de_nata%29_20230409_194702.jpg/500px-Tart_telur_Portugis_%28Past%C3%A9is_de_nata%29_20230409_194702.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pastel de nata (locally known as tart telur Portugis) in Malaysia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATart_telur_Portugis_(Past%C3%A9is_de_nata)_20230409_194702.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Louis15-1.jpg/500px-Louis15-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Louis15-1.jpg/1280px-Louis15-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Louis15-1.jpg/500px-Louis15-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maurice Quentin de La Tour, a bravura pastel portrait of Louis XV, 1748","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALouis15-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Odilon_Redon_%28French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Odilon Redon, Baronne de Domecy, c. 1900, pastel and graphite on light brown laid paper, J. Paul Getty Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOdilon_Redon_(French_-_Baronne_de_Domecy_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg/500px-Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg/1280px-Edgar_DEGAS_La_Danseuse_Rose%2C_Pastel_on_canvas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/E